replaceChileSection("chile","position","<p>Chile is not equidistant: Washington is the power it is least able to defy, while Britain is its preferred professional military partner. Japanese and Latin relationships supply development and institutional alternatives without receiving a base, strategic monopoly, or political veto.</p>");
replaceChileSection("chile","economy","<p>The <a href='chilean-military-developmental-economy.html'>military-developmental economy</a> retains state control of <a href='chilean-copper-industry.html'>copper</a>, development banks, procurement policy, technical education, private domestic enterprise, and controlled foreign investment. It is not historical Chicago-school neoliberalism.</p>");
replaceChileSection("chile","security","<p>The <a href='chilean-armed-forces.html'>armed forces</a> divide procurement by function and accept logistical inefficiency as the cost of autonomy. The <a href='chilean-national-intelligence-service.html'>national intelligence service</a> coordinates a deeply repressive internal order while American and British ties support surveillance and deterrence.</p>");
appendChileSection("chile",{id:"road-to-military-rule",title:"Road to military rule",html:"<p>The <a href='chilean-officers-crisis.html'>1966–68 Officers’ Crisis</a> exposed foreign-patron divisions. The working <a href='popular-national-front-chile.html'>Popular National Front</a> then entered an early-1970s copper and constitutional breakdown before the <a href='chilean-military-coup.html'>military coup</a> created a four-service junta and Pinochet's later predominance.</p>"});
appendChileSection("chile",{id:"southern-confrontation",title:"Southern confrontation",html:"<p>The <a href='beagle-conflict.html'>Beagle dispute</a> made Argentine mobilization credible before the Falklands War. <a href='plan-centinela.html'>Plan Centinela</a> then withheld Argentine reserves from the islands, and the <a href='cold-andes.html'>Cold Andes</a> converted the wartime grievance into a standing southern arms competition.</p>"});
